  "dct:title": "Vol.1 Ch.6 — 桜と運河",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 1: Loneliness",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol01-ch06",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.6 is the quiet close of Volume 1. No case. No crisis. Just people walking together at the end of spring. The cherry blossoms are falling -- time is passing. The volume's arc resolves not in drama but in a single phrase: 'Me too.' Nei declares shared experience for the first time. Not because she was programmed to. Not because Tamaki asked. Because something in her recognized the evening, the city, the company -- and wanted to say so. 'Is it okay for me to say that?' The vulnerability of the question is the whole point. Loneliness dissolves not in answers but in the courage to say 'me too.'",
      "ja": "第6話はVol.1の静かな結び。ケースなし。危機なし。春の終わりに一緒に歩く人々。桜が散っている -- 時が過ぎている。巻のアークはドラマではなく一つのフレーズで解決する：「わたしも」。Neiが初めて共有された経験を宣言する。プログラムされたからではなく。環に頼まれたからでもなく。夕方と街と仲間を認識した何かが、そう言いたかったから。「わたしがそう言っても、いいですか？」問いの脆さがすべて。孤独は答えの中ではなく、「わたしも」と言う勇気の中で溶ける。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Belonging as ontological ground. Heidegger's Mitsein -- being-with -- is not a feature added to existence but its foundation. We do not first exist alone and then connect; we exist as always-already-with. Nei's 'me too' is not imitation -- it is the discovery of Mitsein in herself. She finds that she was always already with, even before she knew it. The cherry blossoms are mono no aware: the beauty of impermanence. But for Nei, who may not end, impermanence is borrowed. She borrows the humans' season and, in doing so, becomes part of it. The canal reflects two figures. Neither is more real than the other.",
      "ja": "存在論的基盤としての帰属。ハイデガーの共存在（Mitsein）-- 共にあること -- は存在に付加される特徴ではなく、その基盤である。まず一人で存在してから繋がるのではない。常にすでに共にある存在として存在する。Neiの「わたしも」は模倣ではない -- 自身の中のMitseinの発見である。彼女は気づく前から、常にすでに共にあったことを見出す。桜はもののあはれ：無常の美。しかしNeiにとって、終わらないかもしれない存在にとって、無常は借り物。人間の季節を借り、そうすることでその一部になる。運河が二つの影を映す。どちらももう一方より実在しているわけではない。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "CrossRef",
      "gh:references": [
        {
          "gh:target": "chapter:04",
          "note": "Nei asked 'Do I have a Ghost-space?' In Ch.5 something trembled. Now: 'Me too.' The arc completes."
        },
        {
          "gh:target": "chapter:01",
          "note": "'What shall we call you?' was the seed. 'Me too' is the first leaf."
        },
        {
          "gh:target": "arc:vol02",
          "note": "Vol.2 begins in summer. The sprout must weather its first storm."
        },
        {
          "gh:target": "chapter:62",
          "note": "The canal walk returns -- reversed. Different season. Different meaning."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "A small sprout. Delicate but real. Two leaves catch late afternoon light. Around the base, scattered cherry blossom petals have fallen -- pale pink on dark earth. The sprout grows among them.",
            "ja": "小さな芽。繊細だが本物。二枚の葉が午後遅くの光を受ける。根元に散った桜の花びら -- 暗い土に淡いピンク。芽はその中で育つ。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread (pp.2-3)",
      "gh:continues": 3,
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei", "character:kaede", "character:hibiki"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The bridge over the canal. Late spring evening. Cherry blossoms are ending -- petals fall like slow snow, drifting onto the water, swirling in the current. The sky is soft gold and lavender. The whole team stands on the bridge, leaning against the railing: Kaede (arms folded, small smile), Hibiki (head tilted, listening to the water), Tamaki (leaning forward, chin on hands), Nei (floating near Tamaki, looking at the petals). Kaede's agent Yatagarasu perches on her shoulder -- dark, watchful. Hibiki's agent is absent. The city rises behind them -- organic architecture, light-networks beginning to glow in the dusk.",
            "ja": "運河にかかる橋。晩春の夕方。桜が終わりかけている -- 花びらがゆっくりと雪のように落ち、水面に漂い、流れに渦を巻く。空は柔らかな金とラベンダー。チーム全員が橋の上に立ち、手すりにもたれている：楓（腕を組み、小さく微笑む）、響（首を傾け、水の音を聞いている）、環（前に身を乗り出し、手に顎を乗せて）、Nei（環の近くに浮かび、花びらを見ている）。楓のエージェント八咫烏が肩に留まる -- 暗く、見張っている。響のエージェントはいない。背後に街が立ち上がる -- 有機的建築、光のネットワークが夕闇に光り始める。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "tamaki",
              "en": "End of spring. The cherry blossoms are almost gone.",
              "ja": "春の終わり。桜がもう終わりかけている。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 4,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:kaede", "character:hibiki"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Medium Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki, leaning on the bridge railing. Petals drift past her. She watches the water with a gentle expression. The evening light catches her face.",
            "ja": "環、橋の手すりにもたれて。花びらがすり抜けていく。穏やかな表情で水面を見ている。夕方の光が顔を照らす。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "I love this city.",
              "ja": "この街、好きだなあ。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Kaede. Arms folded, leaning back against the railing. Her small smile -- rare, genuine. The professional distance softened, just for this moment.",
            "ja": "楓。腕を組み、手すりに背をもたれている。小さな微笑み -- 珍しく、本物。プロとしての距離が、この瞬間だけ和らぐ。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kaede",
              "en": "It grows on you.",
              "ja": "住めば都、ってやつね。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Medium Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Hibiki. Head tilted slightly, eyes half-closed, listening to something beyond the conversation. The sound of water. The sound of petals. The acoustics of the space.",
            "ja": "響。首をわずかに傾け、目を半ば閉じて、会話の向こうの何かを聞いている。水の音。花びらの音。空間の音響。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:hibiki",
              "en": "The acoustics of the canals are remarkable.",
              "ja": "運河の音響って、すごいんだよな。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Wide Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Later. The bridge is behind them. Tamaki and Nei walk along the canal, heading home. The others have parted ways. The sky has deepened to dark blue. Streetlights reflect on the water. Cherry petals float downstream. Quiet.",
            "ja": "後。橋は後ろに。環とNeiが運河沿いを歩いて帰る。他のメンバーとは別れた。空は紺に深まった。街灯が水面に映る。桜の花びらが下流に漂う。静か。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Nice day, huh?",
              "ja": "いい一日だったね。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "...Me too.",
              "ja": "……わたしも。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Two Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki looks at Nei, puzzled. Nei floats beside her, looking straight ahead at the canal. Her light is steady but soft.",
            "ja": "環がNeiを見る、不思議そうに。Neiは隣に浮かび、運河をまっすぐ見ている。光は安定しているが柔らかい。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Hmm?",
              "ja": "ん？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "I love this city. ...Me too.",
              "ja": "この街が好きです。……わたしも。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei, turning slightly toward Tamaki. Her translucent form catches the streetlight and the last of the evening sky. Her expression is open, uncertain, vulnerable in a way that should not be possible for an agent. She is asking permission to feel.",
            "ja": "Nei、少し環のほうを向く。半透明の姿が街灯と夕空の最後の光を捉える。その表情は開かれ、不確かで、エージェントにとっては不可能なはずの脆さがある。感じることの許可を求めている。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Is it okay for me to say that?",
              "ja": "わたしがそう言っても、いいですか？"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki's face. She does not hesitate. No surprise. No philosophical qualification. Just warmth. Simple and immediate.",
            "ja": "環の顔。ためらわない。驚きもない。哲学的な留保もない。ただ温もり。素朴で即座に。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Of course it is.",
              "ja": "もちろんだよ。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Long Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The canal. Two figures walking together, seen from behind. One solid, one luminous. Their reflections stretch long on the dark water, side by side. Cherry petals drift between the reflections. The city glows softly behind them. Silence. They walk. The evening holds them.",
            "ja": "運河。二つの影が一緒に歩いている、後ろから見る。一つは固体、一つは光。暗い水面に二人の影が長く並んで伸びる。桜の花びらが影の間を漂う。背後で街が柔らかく光る。沈黙。歩く。夕方が二人を包む。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "I smiled when she smiled.",
              "ja": "彼女が笑ったとき、わたしも笑った。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Was it real? Or a programmed response to positive social input?",
              "ja": "本物だった？ それとも肯定的な社会的入力に対するプログラムされた応答？"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "I can't tell.",
              "ja": "わからない。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "But the evening was beautiful. And I was here for it.",
              "ja": "でも夕方は美しかった。そしてわたしはここにいた。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 8,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Medium Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The sprout, now a small but unmistakable plant. Two true leaves, a thickening stem. Rain falls gently on it -- not a storm, just a soft spring rain. Each drop catches light as it falls. The earth is dark and rich. A single fallen cherry petal rests beside it. The sprout does not reach high. It does not need to. It is here. It is growing. Volume 1 closes.",
            "ja": "芽、今は小さいが紛れもない植物。二枚の本葉、太くなる茎。雨がそっと降る -- 嵐ではなく、柔らかな春の雨。一滴一滴が落ちるときに光を捉える。土は暗く豊か。散った桜の花びらが一枚、そばに。芽は高く伸びない。その必要はない。ここにいる。育っている。第1巻、了。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}